"FACT CHECK: Did Lindsey Graham Say That Trump ‘Probably Knows More About Medicine’ Than The ‘So-Called Scientists At The NIH And CDC’? | Check Your Fact (https://checkyourfact.com/2020/03/17/fact-check-lindsey-graham-trump-knows-medicine-viruses-scientists-nih-cdc/)\nciteturn10view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.5 years ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://checkyourfact.com/2020/03/17/fact-check-lindsey-graham-trump-knows-medicine-viruses-scientists-nih-cdc/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 53\nL0: \nL1:  【0† †www.facebook.com】 【1† †twitter.com】\nL2: # FACT CHECK: Did Lindsey Graham Say That Trump ‘Probably Knows More About Medicine’ Than The ‘So-Called Scientists At The NIH And CDC’?\nL3: \nL4: 9:06 PM 03/17/2020 Elias Atienza | Senior Reporter\nL5: \nL6:   share on facebook tweet this\nL7: \nL8: An image 【2†shared on Facebook†www.facebook.com】 claims South Carolina Sen. Lindsey Graham said President Donald Trump “probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses” than the “so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC.”\nL9: \nL10: Verdict: False\nL11: There is no record of Graham ever making the comment. It originated in a tweet from a user that has shared fake quotes in the past.\nL12: \nL13: Fact Check:\nL14: \nL15: The 【3†tweet†twitter.com】 that appears to have started the claim has been deleted, but screen grabs of it 【2†continue to circulate†www.facebook.com】 on other social media platforms. 【4†(RELATED: Did Trump Call The Coronavirus A ‘Hoax’ At His South Carolina Rally)】\nL16: “CAPITOL HILL: @LindseyGrahamSC says @realDonaldTrump ‘probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC. If anyone is going to eradicate this plague it’ll be the president,'” the screen grabbed tweet 【2†quotes†www.facebook.com】 Graham as saying.\nL17: The comment would have been picked up by the media if Graham had actually said the words, yet 【5†no news outlets†www.google.com】 have reported on it. The quote does not appear on any of his 【6†social†www.facebook.com】 【7†media†www.instagram.com】 【8†pages†twitter.com】 either.\nL18: Graham did release a 【9†statement†www.lgraham.senate.gov】 Feb. 26 praising the Trump administration’s handling of the coronavirus outbreak. However, at no point did he suggest the president knows more than experts at the National Institutes of Health or the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention.\nL19: “President Trump’s decision to put Vice President Pence in charge of our nation’s efforts to contain the coronavirus is an excellent idea,” reads the 【9†statement†www.lgraham.senate.gov】. “And I have all the confidence in the world that the Vice President and his team will do everything in their power to contain this deadly virus.”\nL20: Dan Lyons, who 【10†describes himself†twitter.com】 as the “inventor of fake news” in his Twitter bio, 【11†tweeted†web.archive.org】 the fabricated quote the same day Graham released that statement. He has shared fake quotes in the past, according to 【12†Snopes†www.snopes.com】.\nL21: \nL22: Multiple Twitter users, including Princeton University history professor Kevin Kruse, 【13†called out†twitter.com】 Lyons for the fake quote attributed to Graham.\nL23: > This is fake. Stop retweeting this account please. 【14†pic.twitter.com/9PEGwRimAV†t.co】\nL24: >\nL25: > — Kevin M. Kruse (@KevinMKruse) 【15†March 2, 2020†twitter.com】\nL26: \nL27: “This is fake,” Kruse 【13†tweeted†twitter.com】. “Stop retweeting this account please.”\nL28: \nL29:   share on facebook tweet this\nL30: # Elias Atienza\nL31: \nL32: ##### Senior Reporter\nL33: \nL34: 【16†Follow Elias on Twitter†twitter.com】 Have a fact check suggestion? Send ideas to 【17†[email protected]】.\nL35: \nL36: 【18† †ifcncodeofprinciples.poynter.org】\nL37: \nL38: ## Trending\nL39: \nL40: 【19†FACT CHECK: Is The US Marine Corps Investigating Susan Crawford For Election Fraud?】\nL41: \nL42:   * 【20†Suggest a fact check】\nL43:   * 【21†About】\nL44:   * 【22†